      "solution": ["Grid: the moves alternate. From frame 1 to 2 the top row moves one cell to the right; from frame 2 to 3 the middle column moves one cell up; the pattern repeats, wrapping round. Next (frame 5 to 6): the top row moves one cell to the right.","Background: grey → white → grey → white → grey. It alternates, so next: white.","Corner marker: top-left → bottom-left → bottom-right → top-right → top-left, one corner anticlockwise each step. Next: bottom-left.","Marker colour: black → white → black → white → black. Next: white."],
      "explanation": "Four independent rules apply: the grid alternates between two shifts (the top row moves one cell to the right, then the middle column moves one cell up); the background alternates; the corner marker moves one corner anticlockwise; the marker colour alternates. Work out each rule from consecutive frames, predict the next frame, then eliminate. Option similarity alone is not evidence of a rule.",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "optionNotes": ["Wrong: the grid uses a shift of column 3 down instead of the next alternating move.","Wrong: the corner marker is at the wrong corner; the background fails to alternate.","Wrong: the grid uses a shift of column 3 down instead of the next alternating move; the marker has the wrong fill.","Correct: the top row moves one cell to the right; background white; marker bottom-left, white.","Wrong: the grid uses a shift of column 3 down instead of the next alternating move; the background fails to alternate."],
