      "solution": ["Grid: the moves alternate. From frame 1 to 2 the middle row moves one cell to the right; from frame 2 to 3 the right column moves one cell up; the pattern repeats, wrapping round. Next (frame 5 to 6): the middle row moves one cell to the right.","Background: white → grey → white → grey → white. It alternates, so next: grey.","Corner marker: bottom-right → top-right → top-left → bottom-left → bottom-right, one corner anticlockwise each step. Next: top-right.","Marker colour: black → white → black → white → black. Next: white."],
      "explanation": "Four independent rules apply: the grid alternates between two shifts (the middle row moves one cell to the right, then the right column moves one cell up); the background alternates; the corner marker moves one corner anticlockwise; the marker colour alternates. Work out each rule from consecutive frames, predict the next frame, then eliminate. Option similarity alone is not evidence of a rule.",
