      "solution": ["use the marker's colour BEFORE a move: white means 3 places anticlockwise; grey or black means 2 places clockwise. Frames 1–6, marker position: upper-left → upper-right → lower-right → top → right → bottom. Next: upper-right.","from frame 2 onward the arrow points 90° clockwise from the previous marker position. Frames 1–6, arrow direction: 90° clockwise from up → 45° clockwise from up → 135° clockwise from up → 225° clockwise from up → 90° clockwise from up → 180° clockwise from up. Next: 270° clockwise from up.","the marker colour cycles grey → black → white and repeats. Frames 1–6, marker colour: grey → black → white → grey → black → white. Next: grey.","the bottom dots cycle 1 → 4 → 3 → 2 and repeat. Frames 1–6, number of bottom dots: 1 → 4 → 3 → 2 → 1 → 4. Next: 3."],
